# Out-of-feed packages, cloned into <openwrt-tree>/package/<name> at a pinned commit.
# Used for packages whose repository is not a feed. Applied by tools/cw-release-build.sh;
# the commit is verified after checkout, so the build fails rather than silently using
# a different one.
#
# Format (whitespace-separated, one package per line):  <name> <git-url> <commit-sha>
#
# Repositories that keep the package in a <name>/ subdirectory (feed layout) are
# installed from that subdirectory; ones with the Makefile at the repo root as a whole.

# luci-app-cw-led: front-panel LED daemon and LuCI page, GPL-2.0-only. Pinned at the commit
# the theme-surface change merged as, on the repository's own default branch. The page's live
# status card takes its panel, hairline and corner radius from the active theme instead of
# painting them itself, and the form styling written for one theme this image no longer ships
# comes out: the form is LuCI's own under every theme.
luci-app-cw-led https://github.com/Pr0Luci/luci-app-cw-led.git a65586cf81aff771d17183405965b40112d7deea
# LuCI theme. One third-party theme ships, so the web UI looks the same on every
# router of this build; it keeps its own package, licence file and pin, and none of
# it is merged into CleanWRT code. LuCI's own Bootstrap theme stays in the image as
# the fallback (configs/arcadyan_aw1000.seed names it, so it is not pinned here).
#
# luci-theme-footstrap: the default theme (files/etc/uci-defaults/96-cw-default-theme).
# Apache-2.0; the package builds its CSS with cat and awk only, so no node toolchain
# enters the builder image. Pinned at the commit tag v0.14.20 points to. The LuCI feed also
# carries a `luci-theme-footstrap` by the same author - an older copy, without the glass
# surfaces and the opacity controls the image's look writes - and one package name is built
# from one recipe only, so the feed's link is removed for the pin to win
# (tools/cw-reset-pinned-package.sh says so on every build).
luci-theme-footstrap https://github.com/VizzleTF/luci-theme-footstrap.git a1711eda02fefe87a12590bae9eaa80c373a4bd9
# luci-app-homeproxy: HomeProxy LuCI app (ImmortalWrt), another proxy app on the same
# cores the image already ships (sing-box). Single-package repo with the Makefile at
# the root, so a local pin and not a feed. Ships DISABLED.
luci-app-homeproxy https://github.com/immortalwrt/homeproxy.git 98a6ad9e71484528008ff435694fd107591f3a1d

# AWvoice: the RJ11 phone port (feed-layout repo; the three packages live at the
# repository root). GPL-2.0-only, the board configuration data file included.
# Pinned at the commit that carries version 1.1.5 of all three packages. It holds the
# SIP side of the phone port - the switch that starts and stops the LAN service this
# image ships, the account a soft phone signs in with, the web phone, and the code a
# phone scans, which files/etc/uci-defaults/49-cw-awvoice-provision-port serves - the
# call log, recordings and the answering machine, the phone book with its rules, and
# quiet hours. Since the 1.1.3 pin it also stands the audio path by when neither a call
# nor a claim needs it, sets a modem left in PCM master mode to slave by itself, lets a
# call go out on either voice domain, holds the page's send level under its ceiling, and
# clears a refused dial so the line does not stay busy. The three packages share one
# version, so they share one pin.
kmod-awvoice-fxs https://github.com/Pr0Luci/openwrt-aw1000-voice-awvoice.git 30d492c044641fa5313f01238e6f42277a6a6dea
awvoice-phoned https://github.com/Pr0Luci/openwrt-aw1000-voice-awvoice.git 30d492c044641fa5313f01238e6f42277a6a6dea
luci-app-awvoice https://github.com/Pr0Luci/openwrt-aw1000-voice-awvoice.git 30d492c044641fa5313f01238e6f42277a6a6dea
